  ["Introductory or Mapping Phase","One-on-One Stage","This phase comes first and usually takes 2-4 sessions. GMAT instructors analyse every student in the batch through interaction and the Mapping Test. This step takes about 10% of total course time."],
  ["Foundation Phase","Batch Stage","Covers the basics of all three GMAT Focus sections: Quantitative, Verbal and Data Insights. This phase is around 20-50% of the whole course."],
  ["Testing Phase","One-on-One Stage","Full-length Computer-Adaptive GMAT Focus mocks and sectional tests. Every course carries a “Minimum Tests” commitment, the minimum number of tests a student must attempt to complete the course."],
  ["Control Phase","One-on-One Stage","The last phase looks into any remaining gaps in test preparation before your exam date."],
];
